{
  "name": "Sneak Attack",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You know how to strike subtly and exploit a foe's distraction. Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack if you have Advantage on the Attack Roll. The attack must use a finesse or a ranged weapon.</p><p>You don't need Advantage on the Attack Roll if another enemy of the target is within 5 feet of it, that enemy isn't Incapacitated, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll.</p><p>The amount of the extra damage increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Sneak Attack column of the Rogue table.</p>",
